  "description": "The top-tier model in the Trigger lineup, engineered with a super-light, triple-butted 6069 alloy frame (approximately 1620 g in size L) that balances strength and featherweight performance\n\nEquipped with a RockShox Recon Gold RL fork with DebonAir and 100 mm travel, delivering smooth control and precision in rough terrain\n\nDriven by a SRAM GX Eagle 1×12 drivetrain featuring a wide-range 10–52 T cassette—sharp, durable, and ready to race\n\nStopping power courtesy of Shimano Deore M6100 hydraulic brakes paired with 180/160 mm rotors—consistent and confident braking\n\nIncludes a KS E‑20i dropper post (120 mm) with remote lever for instant body positioning and downhill control\n\nXC and down‑country optimized geometry—slacker 68° head angle, 430 mm chainstays, long reach, and low standover—ensuring responsive handling and confidence on every terrain\n\nBuilt with internal cable routing, BOOST spacing, and dropper post compatibility, this bike blends clean aesthetics with trail-focused functionality",
